<title>USA: DRS Technologies gets $4.3 mln army contract.</title>
<headline>DRS Technologies gets $4.3 mln army contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>DRS Technologies Inc said Monday a subsidiary has won a $4.3 million contract to supply the U.S. Army with its Multiple Platform Boresight Equipment (MBPE).</p>
<p>The subsidiary, Hauppague, N.Y.-based DRS Photronics Inc, was awarded the contract by the Aviation and Troop Command, the company said. The U.S. Army National Guard and the Aviation Classified Repair Depots will use the systems with AH-1F Cobra helicopters.</p>
<p>The systems help align an aircraft's navigation, targeting and weapon systems with a pilot's sighting gear, DRS said.</p>
